{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And fire came forth from before YHWH and consumed them — it is the same 'and fire came forth' of the first verse. As I explained at וישב משה את דברי העם. And similarly: וישב את הכסף לאמו, which is written twice in the passage of Micah's idol — both are one and the same. So too here, the two verses are one. When the fire came forth and consumed the shelamim on the outer altar, that was when the sons of Aharon took and offered strange fire on the inner altar." "And fire came forth from before YHWH — to burn incense inside first, and it encountered the sons of Aharon there and they died, and afterwards it went forth from there and came to the outer altar and consumed the burnt offering." "And they died before YHWH — and immediately, when Aharon heard, he wanted to stop the service and mourn for his sons."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "Bracketed bet in [ב]בני אהרן reflects editorial reconstruction of a possibly dittographed or damaged word; translated normally as 'the sons of Aharon'."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:31.834608921Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}